{
  "mn96:0.1": "Middle Discourses 96 ",
  "mn96:0.2": "With Esukārī ",
  "mn96:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn96:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn96:2.1": "Then Esukārī the brahmin went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn96:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "mn96:3.1": "“Worthy Gotama, the brahmins prescribe four kinds of service: ",
  "mn96:3.2": "for a brahmin, an aristocrat, a peasant, and a menial. ",
  "mn96:3.3": "This is the service they prescribe for a brahmin: ",
  "mn96:3.4": "‘A brahmin, an aristocrat, a peasant, and a menial may all serve a brahmin.’ ",
  "mn96:3.5": "",
  "mn96:3.6": "This is the service they prescribe for an aristocrat: ",
  "mn96:3.7": "‘An aristocrat, a peasant, and a menial may all serve an aristocrat.’ ",
  "mn96:3.8": "",
  "mn96:3.9": "This is the service they prescribe for a peasant: ",
  "mn96:3.10": "‘A peasant or a menial may serve a peasant.’ ",
  "mn96:3.11": "",
  "mn96:3.12": "This is the service they prescribe for a menial: ",
  "mn96:3.13": "‘Only a menial may serve a menial. ",
  "mn96:3.14": "For who else will serve a menial?’ ",
  "mn96:3.15": "",
  "mn96:3.16": "These are the four kinds of service that the brahmins prescribe. ",
  "mn96:3.17": "What do you say about this?” ",
  "mn96:4.1": "“But brahmin, did the whole world authorize the brahmins